# Override the API base URL only if your setup differs from the default.
#
# Android emulator (default, no override needed):
#   EXPO_PUBLIC_API_BASE_URL=http://10.0.2.2:3000
#
# Physical Android device on the same Wi-Fi — use the dev PC's LAN IP
# (find it with `ipconfig` on Windows, look for IPv4 Address):
#   EXPO_PUBLIC_API_BASE_URL=http://192.168.1.20:3000
#
# Recommended temporary phone workflow (keeps this file's emulator setting intact):
#   .\scripts\start-phone.ps1 -ApiHost 192.168.1.20
#
# iOS simulator:
#   EXPO_PUBLIC_API_BASE_URL=http://localhost:3000
#
# Copy this file to `.env` and uncomment the line you need. `.env` is gitignored.

# ── Google Sign-In ("Continue with Google") ──────────────────────────────────
# The **Web application** OAuth client ID from Google Cloud Console
# (APIs & Services → Credentials). It looks like:
#   1234567890-abcdefghijklmnop.apps.googleusercontent.com
#
# Use the WEB client ID here even on Android. The Android OAuth client still has
# to exist (Google matches it by package name + SHA-1 fingerprint), but the ID
# token's audience is always the web client — which is what the server verifies.
#
# The server must hold the SAME value as GOOGLE_WEB_CLIENT_ID in
# AAROH-Server/api/.env, or every sign-in fails the audience check.
#
# Left unset, the Google button still renders but reports "not configured" when
# tapped instead of failing silently.
#
# EXPO_PUBLIC_GOOGLE_WEB_CLIENT_ID=1234567890-abcdefghijklmnop.apps.googleusercontent.com

# Only needed once the app also targets iOS (the iOS OAuth client ID):
# EXPO_PUBLIC_GOOGLE_IOS_CLIENT_ID=

# NOTE: EXPO_PUBLIC_* values are inlined into the JS bundle at build time, so
# after changing any of them restart the bundler with `npx expo start --clear`.
# Google Sign-In additionally needs a native rebuild (`npx expo run:android`) —
# it does not work in Expo Go.
#
# This file is a TEMPLATE and is committed to git. Expo never reads it — only
# `.env` (and `.env.local`) are loaded. Put real values in `.env`, which is
# gitignored, or the app will keep reporting "not configured" no matter what you
# write here.
